Z||000000||Songman||01-09-2001||09:59 AM||||Once again I am trying to get Fiero owners in Tennessee interested in getting together. I sent out an e-mail to all of the owners registered on F.O.L.D. to see what kind of response I got.<P>Out of the 33 registered owners I got back 8 undeliverable e-mail addresses, 7 positive responses, and the remainder unanswered so far.<P>One of the respondents from Columbia, TN has 52 Fieros! Twenty-three or more of these are running cars. We will soon have a new place to shop for Fiero stuff. They are specializing in 3.8 conversions and kits. Watch for the Fiero Farm soon!<P>I invited all that are not members of this forum to come sign up and talk with us. Anyone from Tennessee that I didn't get from the F.O.L.D. list that is interested, please contact me...<P>My7Fieros, haven't heard from you yet? We need someone from your end of the state!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/icons/icon7.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> ||||reg||7
